  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So with videoplayers i already have an idea, since Youtube-dl can return a JSON Object for the request, what if vrc would add a endpoint to parse that json object so we can get track title, uploader and such meta data infos?\n\nIt would be cool to have access to the Metadata of let's say a YouTube Video, since Youtube-DL can return a JSON Object, by using --dump-json as arguments on YT-DL. Mock up Syscall could look something like this:\n\nyoutube-dl --dump-json --no-check-certificate -f \"mp4[height<=?720]/best[height<=?720]\" --get-url https://youtube.com/watch?v=SOMEVIDEOIDHERE\n\n\nlooking forward to your inputs on this one! \n~M.O.O.N",
